Third-party components

This plugin does not vendor any third-party code. `jarvis setup` and
`jarvis listen enable` install the following into a private Python virtual
environment (~/.local/share/jarvis/venv); each is governed by its own license:

  edge-tts        GPL-3.0     https://github.com/rany2/edge-tts
                  Client for Microsoft Edge's online neural TTS. Speech text is
                  sent to Microsoft; see their terms.
  piper-tts       MIT         https://github.com/rhasspy/piper
                  Offline neural TTS. Voice models (e.g. en_GB-alan-medium) are
                  downloaded from Hugging Face under their own licenses (most are
                  CC-BY or public domain; see each voice's MODEL_CARD).
  openwakeword    Apache-2.0  https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord
                  Wake-word detection; bundles the pretrained "hey_jarvis" model.
  onnxruntime     MIT         https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  numpy           BSD-3       https://numpy.org

Runtime dependencies expected on the system (not installed by this plugin):

  Quickshell      LGPL-3.0    https://quickshell.org        (bar widget, visualizer)
  mpv             GPL-2.0+    https://mpv.io                (playback; ffplay/pw-play also work)
  PipeWire        MIT         https://pipewire.org          (pw-record for the wake word)
  Voxtype         MIT         https://github.com/peteonrails/voxtype
                  Optional; the default dictation target for "Hey Jarvis".
  espeak-ng       GPL-3.0     https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
                  Optional last-resort TTS engine.
